(# Site Emergency Response Plan) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Fire Emergency) Tj
T* (On discovering a fire, activate the nearest pull station and evacuate using the nearest marked) Tj
T* (exit. Do not use elevators. Fire extinguishers are for small, contained fires only; if the fire) Tj
T* (grows beyond the size of a trash can, evacuate immediately. The fire brigade assembles at the) Tj
T* (north gate to brief arriving responders. Department heads confirm their area is clear before) Tj
T* (leaving the building and report the status to the fire brigade leader at the assembly point.) Tj
T* (Re-entry is permitted only after the fire department gives an explicit all-clear.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Chemical Spill) Tj
T* (Small spills under 1 liter may be contained by trained staff using the spill kits located at) Tj
T* (each dock bay and the chemical storage room. Spills larger than 1 liter, or any spill involving) Tj
T* (an unknown substance, require full evacuation of the affected zone and notification of the site) Tj
T* (safety officer. Ventilation in the affected zone should be increased where safe to do so, and) Tj
T* (the safety data sheet for the spilled material must be pulled and handed to responders on) Tj
T* (arrival.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
7 0 obj
<< /Length 957 >>
stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
14 TL
72 740 Td
(## Medical Emergency) Tj
T* (Call the site emergency line first, then begin first aid only if trained to do so. Automated) Tj
T* (external defibrillators are mounted near the break room and the main warehouse entrance. Do not) Tj
T* (move a seriously injured person unless they are in immediate danger. Someone should be sent to) Tj
T* (the nearest access road to flag down arriving emergency medical services and guide them) Tj
T* (directly to the casualty.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Severe Weather) Tj
T* (During a severe weather warning, all personnel move to the designated shelter areas in the) Tj
T* (central corridor, away from exterior windows and large roof spans. Remain sheltered until the) Tj
T* (all-clear is announced over the site paging system. Forklift and crane operations must stop) Tj
T* (immediately once a warning is issued, and outdoor contractors must be accounted for along with) Tj
T* (regular staff.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
8 0 obj
<< /Length 1578 >>
stream
BT
/F1 12 Tf
14 TL
72 740 Td
(## Evacuation Assembly Points) Tj
T* (Warehouse staff assemble at the north parking lot. Office staff assemble at the south) Tj
T* (courtyard. Shift supervisors take a headcount against the shift roster and report the result to) Tj
T* (the site safety officer within five minutes of evacuation. Visitors and contractors are) Tj
T* (accounted for using the sign-in log from the front desk, which the receptionist brings to the) Tj
T* (assembly point as part of the evacuation procedure. Anyone unaccounted for after the headcount) Tj
T* (is reported to the fire brigade leader immediately so responders can begin a targeted search) Tj
T* (rather than a blind sweep of the building.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This plan is reviewed annually and after any incident requiring a full site evacuation, and) Tj
T* (every department head completes a refresher briefing with their team at each review cycle. New) Tj
T* (hires receive a walkthrough of their nearest exit routes and assembly point on their first day,) Tj
T* (before they are assigned to a work area.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Chain of Command) Tj
T* (The senior manager on site acts as incident commander until the fire department or emergency) Tj
T* (medical services arrive and assume control. If the senior manager is unreachable, the shift) Tj
T* (supervisor with the longest tenure on site takes over the role and briefs the incoming) Tj
T* (commander on what has been done so far, including whether the building has been fully evacuated) Tj
T* (and whether anyone is known to be unaccounted for.) Tj
ET
endstream
